  "title": "Treaty of Brest-Litovsk",
  "summary": "On 3 March 1918 Soviet Russia signed a separate peace at Brest-Litovsk with Germany, Austria-Hungary, Bulgaria and Turkey. Territory west of an agreed line ceased to be under Russian sovereignty, and Russia had to make peace with the Ukrainian People's Republic. World History Encyclopedia puts the loss at about 290,000 square miles; the Allies treated the treaty as void after the November 1918 armistice.",
